// claim: `##.x` Float, `###x` Int (round),
// claim: `##!x` Int (truncate). Three doors, one per result: `0x|v|`, `0d|v|`, `0o|v|`, `0b|v|` give the
// claim: text in that base (`0d|'A'|` is `"0d65"`), the bare bars `|v|` the character (`|65|` and `|"0x41"|`
// claim: are `'A'`), and `#|v|` the number (`#|'A'|` is `65`); a code with no character is an error.
x = 2.7
n = 65
>> ###x ¶             // → 3
>> ##!x ¶             // → 2
>> ##.n + 0.5 ¶       // → 65.5
>> 0d|'A'| ¶          // → 0d65
>> 0x|'A'| ¶          // → 0x41
>> |n| ¶              // → A
>> |"0x41"| ¶         // → A
>> #|'A'| ¶           // → 65
